---
# The one door that lets monitor-bridge (daniel-server) query this cluster's Prometheus.
#
# Slice 3, D8. Prometheus' node-side listener is pinned to 127.0.0.1 by claude_otel_query_host_ip
# — deliberately, so `otelq` can reach it while the LAN cannot — and its Service is ClusterIP.
# Both are correct and neither is changed here: monitor-bridge runs on daniel-server, so it can
# reach neither, and the k3s API server's own :6443 is firewalled off from daniel-server too
# (measured 2026-08-07: connect fails outright). This route is the deliberate exception.
#
# Modelled on the n8n-monitoring route (roles/k8s/n8n/templates/ingressroute.yaml.j2), which
# exists for exactly this problem and is the pattern to copy rather than invent from: LAN-only
# host, matched paths only, rate-limited.
#
# NARROW ON PURPOSE — three separate reasons this is a query-only door:
#   1. PathPrefix `/api/v1/query` is the ONLY path check.py fetches (check.py:644 and :658 both
#      call _instant_query(PROM_URL, "/api/v1/query", ...)). It also admits /api/v1/query_range,
#      which is a prefix match and is likewise read-only.
#   2. Prometheus' admin API (/api/v1/admin/tsdb/delete_series) requires --web.enable-admin-api
#      and the lifecycle endpoints (/-/reload, /-/quit) require --web.enable-lifecycle. Neither
#      flag is set on the Deployment, so those endpoints do not exist to be reached.
#   3. No `/graph`, `/targets` or `/metrics`. Browsing the TSDB is Grafana's job and it already
#      has an authenticated route.
#
# LAN-ONLY, and unlike the shared ingressroute() macro this does NOT honour k8s_public_route.
# That is intentional: when slice 6 flips that flag for the app routes, this one must not follow
# them onto the public internet. There is no authentication in front of it — the guard is that
# the hostname resolves only on the LAN and the paths are read-only.
apiVersion: traefik.io/v1alpha1
kind: IngressRoute
metadata:
  name: prometheus-monitoring
  namespace: {{ k8s_observability_namespace }}
spec:
  entryPoints:
    - https
  routes:
    - kind: Rule
      match: "Host(`prometheus{{ k8s_hostname_suffix }}.local.{{ domain }}`) && PathPrefix(`/api/v1/query`)"
      middlewares:
        - name: rate-limit
      services:
        - name: prometheus
          port: 9090
  tls:
    certResolver: cloudflare
    options:
      name: modern
    domains:
      - main: "{{ domain }}"
        sans:
          - "*.{{ domain }}"
          - "*.local.{{ domain }}"
